1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,792
Calendar Reminders show a reminder on screen before an event starts, and keep

2
00:00:05,792 --> 00:00:07,870
it there until you dismiss it.

3
00:00:07,870 --> 00:00:11,680
This video shows how to set a reminder on an event, who sees

4
00:00:11,680 --> 00:00:16,530
it, what it looks like, and the workflow events that fire at the same moments.

5
00:00:21,130 --> 00:00:24,360
When you are busy in another part of the site, it is easy

6
00:00:24,360 --> 00:00:26,770
to miss that a meeting is about to start.

7
00:00:27,520 --> 00:00:32,101
With the Calendar Reminders feature turned on, an event can remind you on

8
00:00:32,101 --> 00:00:35,870
screen before it starts, on every admin page you have open.

9
00:00:36,620 --> 00:00:40,676
The reminder stays until you dismiss it, so you cannot miss it just

10
00:00:40,676 --> 00:00:42,620
by looking away for a moment.

11
00:00:43,370 --> 00:00:49,195
The calendar's owner is reminded, and so is each invited user who has not declined.

12
00:00:49,195 --> 00:00:53,450
On someone else's calendar, only the people invited see it.

13
00:00:57,628 --> 00:01:01,420
Open Calendars, then Calendar, and choose New event.

14
00:01:01,420 --> 00:01:04,688
Pick your own calendar and the Meeting kind.

15
00:01:05,144 --> 00:01:08,935
Give the event a title, and start it a few minutes from now.

16
00:01:08,935 --> 00:01:14,334
On the General card, the Remind setting says how long before the start to remind people.

17
00:01:14,785 --> 00:01:19,603
You can choose No reminder, When it starts, 5, 10, 15 or 30

18
00:01:19,603 --> 00:01:23,976
minutes before, 1 or 2 hours before, or 1 day before.

19
00:01:23,976 --> 00:01:29,757
An event that takes time reminds 10 minutes before unless you change it.

20
00:01:29,757 --> 00:01:32,425
Here, choose 5 minutes before.

21
00:01:32,876 --> 00:01:34,009
Choose Save.

22
00:01:34,009 --> 00:01:36,652
The reminder now waits for its time.

23
00:01:36,652 --> 00:01:38,856
All-day events do not remind.

24
00:01:43,056 --> 00:01:46,075
Open pages check for reminders every minute.

25
00:01:46,075 --> 00:01:50,059
When the reminder is due, it appears at the top right of the

26
00:01:50,059 --> 00:01:52,896
page, and says how soon the event starts.

27
00:01:53,827 --> 00:01:57,455
It shows on every admin page of the calendar's owner.

28
00:01:57,455 --> 00:02:00,407
Go to another page, and it is still there.

29
00:02:00,858 --> 00:02:04,218
Choose Open calendar to see the event on its day.

30
00:02:04,669 --> 00:02:07,644
Choose Dismiss, and the reminder is gone.

31
00:02:07,644 --> 00:02:13,089
Dismissing it on one page removes it from every other page and tab that is open.

32
00:02:17,289 --> 00:02:21,180
Calendar Reminders also runs in the background every minute.

33
00:02:21,180 --> 00:02:25,012
It notices when an event is about to start, and when it has

34
00:02:25,012 --> 00:02:28,019
ended, once for each occurrence of the event.

35
00:02:28,769 --> 00:02:33,532
A workflow can start at those moments, with the Calendar Event Starting Soon

36
00:02:33,532 --> 00:02:39,109
event, where you set the minutes before the start, and the Calendar Event Completed event.

37
00:02:39,859 --> 00:02:44,373
For example, email the attendees fifteen minutes before a meeting.

38
00:02:44,373 --> 00:02:51,019
Building workflows with calendar events is covered in the video about calendars in workflows and AI.

39
00:02:53,019 --> 00:02:56,955
Set the Remind setting on an event, and its people see a reminder

40
00:02:56,955 --> 00:02:59,117
that stays until they dismiss it.

41
00:02:59,117 --> 00:03:00,559
Thanks for watching.

